Notebook[{
Cell["Elementary CA: additivity vs. fractal dimension", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d6ab967c-419b-487b-8a61-208c5885a155"],

Cell["Wolfram Scientist \[LongDash] research/eca-additivity-fractality", \
"Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"9410a81c-795c-443a-9156-a04da09c662f"],

Cell["Question", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cf499ba3-aeaf-4d1b-abc0-e72b43e4f94c"],

Cell["\<\
Which elementary CA rules produce nested (fractal) single-seed patterns, and \
does additivity (GF(2)-linearity) predict it?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f06600c2-82a7-4591-931b-b306360b763d"],

Cell["Key result", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"962b2e1d-dbf8-4b5d-b0df-b9deac47b95b"],

Cell["\<\
The 8 additive rules split across dimensions {0, 1, log2 3, 1.696}. Eight \
NON-additive rules also reach dim = log2 3; seven collapse onto rule 90 on \
the single-seed orbit, but rule 22 does not \[LongDash] a genuine outlier \
(exact mass 3^k, distinct pattern).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2357e1a1-ae5d-4a65-b893-e20642639851"],

